<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shanghai French Concession</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1849">1849</a>–<a href="/years/1943">1943</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a> French Concession was a foreign concession in Shanghai under French administration from 1849 to 1943. Outside Chinese jurisdiction, it became a refuge for political activists: the Korean Provisional Government was founded there in 1919, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-communist-party">Chinese Communist Party</a> held its first congress there in 1921. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> gave it up to the Japanese-backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-jingwei">Wang Jingwei</a> government in 1943.</p></div>
